<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan State Oil up 1.19 pct.</title>
<headline>Pakistan State Oil up 1.19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan State Oil (PSO) jumped 4.0 rupees, or 1.19 percent, to 340 in early Monday trade due to windfall inventory gains after last week's 7.86 percent devaluation of the rupee, dealers said.</p>
<p>Some 1,600 PSO shares changed hands in early trade.</p>
<p>Dealer Hina Akhlaq said the devaluation worked to PSO's advantage because it places buying orders in advance in dollars.</p>
<p>&quot;The difference in the rupee as a result of the devaluation are its gains,&quot; she said, adding that last week's government announcement of a 10 percent rise in oil product prices was also pushing up energy stocks.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
